i got asked what my best advice for  achieving success on the internet was  the other day  it got me thinking about where the  biggest competitive advantages lie  and i realized something consistency is  even rarer  than talent or enthusiasm think about  yourself  how many times have you had a burst of  enthusiasm for a side hustle you can't  sleep because you're always thinking  about it you watch every youtube video  on the internet  and you're totally submerged in 24 7  keenness this is  essentially every january 1st in the gym  or  final week before launching a new  business or  think to when you started a new project  and realized  that you actually have a natural talent  for it you pick up  ad optimization really easily in your  first class  or you start a podcast and discover that  making the conversation  flow well just comes naturally to you  these situations  come along less frequently than you  might think  but probably more frequently than you  might predict  the problem is they appear randomly  for all your competitors too everyone  else also  stumbles upon a natural capacity for a  new project  and enjoys the benefits of spurts of  enthusiasm a competitive advantage  is not an advantage if the rest of the  competition  has equal access to it another problem  is that  both talent and enthusiasm are only  fleetingly useful  talent might mean you can pick up ad  optimization  20 quicker than everyone else but  as you climb up the ladder you're now  competing with people  who can pick up things just as quickly  and they've been doing it for a decade  enthusiasm might mean you're super  excited to start your podcast and have  researched and organized all your guests  for the next month but after  three months when the plays have  flattened out your enthusiasm is  starting to wane  and you don't control when it comes back  in my experience consistency is the most  valuable  and least common trait of all doing  something challenging  and worthwhile at the same time every  day  or multiple times per week is incredibly  rare it's seen as the realm of  professional athletes  top flight musicians and zen masters and  this  is why consistency is the perfect  competitive advantage opportunity a  higher number  of your competitors will be talented or  enthusiastic  than consistent this means that simply  by not  stopping you will separate yourself  from everyone else imagine that there's  a particular  great filter which all people in your  industry encounter  a big barrier of discomfort perhaps it's  boredom perhaps it's demotivation  perhaps it's slow growth of revenue or  followers  let's say that after 150 weeks of  consistency  the average person in your industry is  really  starting to run out of gas and struggle  their talent and enthusiasm  have both been competed out by other  talented and enthusiastic people  it now becomes a battle of consistency  who can deal with that discomfort and  just  keep going inevitably some competitors  start to drop  off because it's hard and repetitive and  unrewarding  this is why not stopping separates you  from everyone else  consistency is hard and rare sometimes  in the back of your head you might hear  a voice that says  if it was meant to be it wouldn't be  this difficult i shouldn't be finding it  this hard  all my competitors seem to be coping  just fine in  my experience this is untrue everyone  finds consistency difficult they just  don't post  about unremarkable grinding because  there's no magnificence in turning up  every day as brian green says the moment  to moment  of almost anything you are doing is a  grind  it is only upon completion in reflection  when you can see the glory in atomic  habits  james clear asked the head of the  chinese weightlifting team  what sets the world champions apart from  everyone else the answer was simple  whoever can handle the boredom  of daily training the best forget  any ideas you have around consistency  not  being hard the discomfort is a feature  not a bug it's simply a case of dealing  with it  better than the next guy the ability to  be consistent  is getting more valuable as attention  becomes more scarce  and alternative options more abundant if  you're a  peasant in the middle ages it's an easy  decision to become a master woodworker  if the choice is between woodwork and  starving to death  in the 21st century you can gig  economy telegram chat tinder swipe your  way from  half-baked business to semi-launched  project  for an entire career fewer and fewer  people  will be able to consistently do one  thing  for long periods of time this is why  consistency  is the ultimate competitive advantage it  is becoming both  increasingly valued and increasingly  rare  at the same time a final advantage of  consistency  is that you're in control of it you  don't get to choose your talents  or your motivation level but  turning up every day is entirely within  your power  and by doing that you will develop  your talents and build motivation anyway  over time you will end up in a place  you're worthy of as charlie munger says  spend  each day trying to be a little wiser  than you were when you woke up  discharge your duties faithfully and  well systematically you get ahead  but not necessarily in fast spurts  nevertheless  you build discipline by preparing for  fast spurts  slug it out one inch at a time day by  day  at the end of the day if you live long  enough  most people get what they deserve it  takes  10 years to become an overnight success  just keep going and if it came easily  it wouldn't be worth anything anyway so  don't pray for talent or enthusiasm  pray for the strength to keep going let  me know what you think in the comments  below  and for more life lessons press  subscribe peace  [Music]  you
 

